EXT. ROOFTOP APIARY - GOLDEN HOUR

Hives like pastel filing cabinets. Bees drift over the city skyline. A string of bulbs sways overhead.

AMARA OKEKE (30s, veil pushed back, honey on her wrist) lifts a frame heavy with comb. THEO BALASUBRAMANIAN (30s, borrowed veil, delighted) stands too close, holding a smoker he has not lit.

AMARA
Step back.

THEO
I'm fine.

AMARA
You're stepping on the queen's door.

THEO
I'm sorry, Your Majesty.

She laughs. He lights the smoker. A white plume.

AMARA
Gently.

THEO
Always.

The stairwell door bangs. GRANDMOTHER NNEKA (80s, floral housecoat, cane, a shopping bag) hobbles onto the roof.

NNEKA
Amara!

AMARA
Mama?

THEO
Hello, ma'am.

NNEKA
Who is the boy?

AMARA
It's Theo, Mama. I told you.

NNEKA
You told me Thursday.

THEO
Today is Thursday.

NNEKA
Then I am on time.

She sets the bag on a hive. Amara lunges to catch it.

AMARA
Mama! Not there.

NNEKA
It's only plantains.

THEO
They'll love the plantains.

NNEKA
They better. Come, boy. Eat.
